  <diagram name="C4 L3 Terraform components - privately accessible" id="c4-terraform-components">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1000" dy="830" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1000" pageHeight="830" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" parent="1" vertex="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:20px&quot;&gt;Privately accessible static website&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:14px;color:#b8321f&quot;&gt;C4 level 3: Components of the Terraform stack&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#1c1c1c;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="10" width="960.0" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="description" parent="1" vertex="1" value="A platform engineer runs tf.sh or tf.ps1 with the environment&amp;#x27;s terraform.tfvars and backend.hcl. The root module composes eight modules: naming, network, static-web-app, private-endpoint, entra-app-auth, monitoring, monitor-private-link and availability-probe, and renders the APEX sign-in config into outputs. Dashed modules exist only when enable_monitoring is on, which it always is in prod." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5c5c5c;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="62" width="960.0" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Platform engineer&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#5c5c5c&quot;&gt;Runs plans and applies&lt;/span&gt;" style="shape=image;html=1;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;labelPosition=center;align=center;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1c1c1c;spacingTop=6;image=data:image/svg+xml,;" vertex="1">
